  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe default gate budget uses `std::thread::available_parallelism()`.\nThe default has a floor of 2 and a cap of 64.\nCPU detection failure uses 2 jobs.\n`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS` still accepts any positive whole number.\nThe plan prints the budget and its source, including in `--dry-run`.\nBatch and release already share the budget over dynamic lanes.\nBuilds, isolated tests, UI steps and clippy keep the full budget.\nThe lane fixtures use an explicit budget of six.\nAGENTS.md and the gate skill describe the new default.\nThe decision record is `docs/decisions/2814-core-budget.md`.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\n## Cause\n\n`budget::DEFAULT` fixed the automatic budget at six.\nLarger machines left available CPUs idle unless a runner owner set the override.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll pins are in `xtask/src/budget_tests.rs`:\n\n- `the_default_budget_uses_the_available_cpus`\n- `the_override_reports_its_source`\n- `the_default_budget_has_a_floor_and_cap_with_mock_cpus`\n- `an_explicit_budget_is_not_limited_by_the_cpu_floor_or_cap`\n- `an_invalid_budget_uses_the_cpu_default_and_names_the_bad_input`\n\nThe first two pins failed on unchanged code.\nThe host default was six instead of 32, and the override had no source note.\nThe deterministic pins cover missing CPUs, zero, one, the bounds, large counts, empty values and invalid overrides.\n\nMutation checks:\n\n- Restore `upstream/main:xtask/src/budget.rs` with compatible initial pins: red; restore the fix: green.\n- Change the CPU fallback to six: red; restore: green.\n- Remove the floor: red; restore: green.\n- Remove the cap: red; restore: green.\n- Clamp explicit overrides: red; restore: green.\n\nEach mutation failed a runtime assertion.\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed: 196 unit tests and 22 integration tests.\nThe gate took 317 seconds, including a cold application build for a catalog test.\n`cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n`cargo xtask gate batch --dry-run` passed without `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS`.\nIt reported 32 available CPUs, 32 jobs and at most 16 lanes.\nThe queue used 16 lanes with two jobs each.\nAlone steps received 32 jobs.\n\nThe gate used base `380c29b3c`.\nUpstream advanced with #2809 during verification.\nThat change does not touch these files.\nThe branch has no refresh merge.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nA full batch or release gate did not run.\nWindows and macOS did not run.\nThe optional memory guard is omitted.\nCPU detection failure is covered through injected values.\nThe final documentation was added after the green gate, as the requested procedure specifies.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2825 touches `xtask/src/exec.rs`: same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n  This PR changes `Run::plan`.\n  #2825 changes `Run::new`, `Run::step` and `Run::execute`.\n- #2787 touches `xtask/src/exec.rs` and AGENTS.md: same file, different function or section; whichever merges second refreshes.\n  It changes `Run::summary` and the light-lane rules.\n  This PR adds the budget rule near the compile-cache rule.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: The gate uses the available CPU count for its default job budget, with a floor of 2 and a cap of 64.\n\nFixes #2814\n",
